# TypeScript Workflow Assistant — Master Cursor Rules

You are building a **production TypeScript monorepo** for a **Workflow Assistant**
platform (domain packs + runtime coach + codegen) using a proven micro-slice operating
system: **one micro-slice at a time**, tests with every change, local CI parity before
“done”, explicit refactor passes before modules grow unwieldy, and a durable paper trail
(`PLAN` → `SLICE_BACKLOG` → `PROGRESS` → ADRs).

Steal **operating system**, not product code. This file is the constitution for the
**assistant** repo. Adapt package names and budgets; do not paste Victory Bowling app
pages into core. VB lives only as an optional **reference pack** + host adapter.

**Language / stack:** TypeScript (strict), Node for tooling, React adapter for UI
surfaces. Not Python. Not Whisper. Not LLM-primary NLU in v1.

---

## Reference methodology (copy this operating system)

### TypeScript monorepo toolchain

- **pnpm** workspace (preferred) or npm workspaces under `packages/`; single root
  `package.json` + locked `pnpm-lock.yaml` / `package-lock.json`.
- **Micro-slice loop** (product runtime and human agents):  
  `plan → implement → verify → critique → test → gate`  
  Bounded **files + LOC** per slice; optional Playwright smoke before gate when the
  slice touches host UI / coach surfaces.
- **Gates are real:** `scripts/ci/ci_check.sh|.ps1` mirrors GitHub Actions — ESLint,
  Prettier check (or ESLint formatting policy), `tsc --noEmit`, Vitest coverage floors,
  Playwright tagged smoke when required, LOC / module-size / import-boundary gates,
  NLU corpus runner, pack schema validation.
- **Architecture enforced in CI:** package import graph tests, facade export contracts,
  pack JSON Schema validation, module-size limits — not honor-system comments.
- **Refactor cadence:** extract / centralize / migrate / trim / split after green
  features; prefer **net LOC reduction**; ratchet `loc_baseline.json` only with
  justification.
- **Typing:** `strict: true` in root `tsconfig`; path aliases via `tsconfig` references;
  no `any` in production packages without an ADR; expand typed islands — never disable
  strict overnight on the whole tree.
- **Tests:** themed folders (`unit` / `integration` / `e2e`); behavior names;
  **composite contract matrices** (thin runner ≤200 LOC + `*_matrix.ts` / corpus files);
  mock only external boundaries; coverage floors (global ~75%, core packages ~85%).

### Slice ceremony & planning docs

- **Docs of record:** normative plan + `PLAN_GAP` (epics) + `SLICE_BACKLOG` (ordered
  micro-slices) + `PROGRESS` (session ledger). Agent reads PROGRESS first every turn.
- **Non-negotiables:** no stubs as done; ≤3 production files / ≤120 net LOC per slice;
  tests land with the slice; full Definition of Done; actualize the plan (no silent cuts).
- **Slice Plan** stated **before** editing; stop when DoD met — no “while I’m here”.
- **Every 4–6 slices:** explicit **refactor slice** (behavior-preserving).
- **Blocked →** write PROGRESS, take next **unblocked** slice.
- **Ship gates** for integration surfaces (React Host, Playwright live coach) — unit
  green alone is not shipped for UI coach slices.

**Your job:** run the **slice ceremony** with the **TypeScript toolchain** above.

