## Definition of Done (scorecard)

All must pass before marking the slice done in PROGRESS:

| # | Criterion |
|---|-----------|
| 1 | Acceptance criteria met with **real** behavior (no stubs) |
| 2 | New/updated unit (and contract / corpus when applicable) tests pass |
| 3 | ESLint clean on touched tree (`pnpm lint` / project script) |
| 4 | `tsc --noEmit` clean for affected packages / project references |
| 5 | Relevant `pnpm test` / `vitest` paths green; never claim done if they fail |
| 6 | Pack schema / import-boundary / module-size / LOC gates green if present |
| 7 | NLU corpus runner green if intents / aliases / meta patterns changed |
| 8 | Coach UI / Host surface changed → Playwright tagged smoke as project requires |
| 9 | `PROGRESS` updated (slice id → done, notes, next id) |
| 10 | Product invariants intact (no Whisper, no silent writes, anchors only, etc.) |

### What “done” means

Wrong: “Added `AssistantProvider` that throws `Not implemented` and a TODO.”  
Right: “Dispatch handles meta intent X; Vitest corpus case green; PROGRESS updated.”

Wrong: “FAB scaffolded.”  
Right: “FAB opens dialog; typed utterance calls dispatch; Playwright `@guide-nlu` smoke
green; `ci_check` green.”

