## Domain pack contract (assistant-specific)

A pack must be able to declare (names illustrative; freeze via JSON Schema + ADR):

| Object | Role |
|--------|------|
| Flow steps | id, title, kind, requires[], prefers[], keywords[], hideWhen[] |
| Controls | stable guide ids, roles (cta/field/tab/nav/row) |
| Nav skips | step → path template, modal key, spotlight id |
| Intents | step aliases, meta intents, slot schemas |
| Completeness | bindings against RuntimeContext |
| Glossary / lexicons | explain-field and domain lookup |
| Corpus | utterance → expected intent/step/slots |

**Wire-up checklist when adding a step** (DoD for pack slices):

1. Flow step + requires  
2. Completeness binding  
3. Nav-skip resolve  
4. Intent aliases + corpus cases  
5. Guide ids + host annotation instructions / demo host mounts  
6. `notifyStepCompleted` (or equivalent) on the save path that finishes the step  

